n mr mizigoy because  literally none of that ever happens ever  and that of course is my big problem  with these libertarians they're living  in a fantasy land  well if we just let corporations do  whatever of course they're going to take  care of people  of course they're going to lower prices  hello what what on earth like what drugs  do you have to be on  to make you have visions of this world  where corporations inherently do the  right thing  they don't  even with government agencies that are  supposed to force them to do the right  thing they still don't do the right  thing  what i would encourage all of these  libertarians in the united states to do  is go get a job at a plaintiff's law  firm and work there for at least a year  see i've worked with a plaintiff's law  firm including actually other law firms  all throughout the country as well  for almost two straight decades  i have seen some of the worst documents  imaginable  from every industry imaginable  whether it's the tobacco industry the  fossil fuel the chemical industry  food companies  they will literally never do the right  thing unless they are forced to pay up  for it  and when that happens they typically  only do the right thing while they think  people are still paying attention then  they go right back to doing horrible  things  so again libertarians i beg you  read some corporate documents  then get back to me  on whether or not you think corporations  will inherently do the right thing  for the american public  and you know what while we're talking  about some of the stupidest things  imaginable that a human being can say  let's talk about herschel walker right  herschel walker  this week  came out  in his opposition to the inflation  reduction act and i'm so sorry it's so  hard to keep a straight face and do this  sometimes  and he said that uh you know  we don't need additional spending on  environmental issues  because aren't there enough trees  already  let me let me read let me read hi